Ha, the black-and-white warning is exactly the sort of thing that makes me want to buy the chocolate just to spite it, and I'm not proud of that.

I'd go for the Galaxy. It's mid-afternoon, I've had a cup of tea and nothing much else, and I'd rather have something sweet than crisps.

{"choice": 10}

Mid-afternoon, a vending machine, and those warning labels on everything sugary; I'd grumble at the label before anything else, but I'm diabetic and the nurse has been on at me, so I'd probably go for the cheap salty thing I actually fancy.

I'd buy the McCoy's salt and vinegar crisps. I haven't touched crisps since the diabetes, but honestly a bag of those is what my hand would go for, and I'd feel a bit guilty eating them in the car on the way back from the school gate.

